// HandOnSoftwareProjectWithBody Hand on a software project
//
// WHO LOOKS AFTER IT changes to another member of the account environment, who takes
// Administrator on the project with it. The one before steps down: their access on the project
// becomes Editor, a share they were given included, because a person holds one grant on a
// project (decision 0650). When the folder is their own, they still own it, so they keep full
// rights over the project for as long as the folder is theirs.
//
// HANDING IT TO THE PERSON WHO LOOKS AFTER IT NOW CHANGES NOTHING and refuses nothing.
//
// SOMEONE WHO IS NOT A MEMBER IS REFUSED with a 422 on `/body/person_id`, code `not_a_member`.
// An unmarked project is not handed on: 409 `software_project_unmarked`.
//
// A LEAVER'S REASSIGN ASK IS CLOSED BY IT. When the member who looked after the project left,
// the project carries one ask, a task of the kind `software:reassign`; handing the project on
// finishes that task, as the person handing it on, and closes the ask. The task is finished
// first: when the task service could not be asked, the answer is 503 `tasks_unavailable`,
// nothing is handed on, and the same request can be sent again.
//
