	// MarkOwnFolderAsSoftwareProjectWithBodyWithResponse Mark a folder of your own as a software project
	//
	// A STORAGE FOLDER BECOMES A SOFTWARE PROJECT. Any folder of your own, a nested one too. The
	// code stays in it, with Storage keeping its versions; Software never moves, renames or copies
	// it.
	//
	// TWO PERMISSIONS, EACH ASKED OF ITS OWN OBJECT. "Mark a folder as a software project" is asked
	// of the account environment, and the right to share the folder in Storage is asked of the
	// folder: sharing is asked, not just reading, because marking lets the project's viewers see
	// what is built from the code. A refusal is one 403.
	//
	// WHOEVER MARKS IT HOLDS ADMINISTRATOR ON THE PROJECT, and looks after it, until it is handed
	// on. A folder of your own is yours, so the project is yours too.
